fix(anthropic): fall back to auto tool choice with manual thinking (#23332)

## Background

https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/23321

Previously, combining manual thinking with a forced tool choice sent an
invalid request to Anthropic, causing HTTP 400.

## Summary

manual thinking now uses the existing auto fallback with a warning

extended the existing fallback:
- Named tool: send only that tool with `tool_choice: auto`.
- Required tool: keep all tools, use `auto`.
- Emit a warning because tool use is no longer guaranteed

## End-to-End Verification

verified by running the example: 

<details>

```ts
import { anthropic } from '@ai-sdk/anthropic';
import { generateText, tool } from 'ai';
import * as z from 'zod/v4';
import { run } from '../../lib/run';

run(async () => {
  await generateText({
    model: anthropic('claude-haiku-4-5'),
    providerOptions: {
      anthropic: { thinking: { type: 'enabled', budgetTokens: 5000 } },
    },
    tools: {
      lookup: tool({
        description: 'Look something up',
        inputSchema: z.object({ query: z.string() }),
        execute: async ({ query }) => ({ result: query }),
      }),
    },
    toolChoice: { type: 'tool', toolName: 'lookup' },
    prompt: 'Look up the latest ECB rate decision.',
  });
});
```

</details>

