fix(openai): preserve detected language codes in transcription responses (#23589)

## Background

https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/23490

OpenAI transcription responses containing `languages: [{ code: 'en' }]`
or `anguage: 'en'` returned `language: undefined`, silently dropping
detected language information

## Summary

- Preserve two-letter language codes and existing language-name
conversion.
- Populate language from a single detected language.
- Expose the full array through providerMetadata.openai.languages,
preserving multilingual results without selecting an arbitrary language

## End-to-End Verification

verified by running the repro:

<details>

```ts
import { createOpenAI } from '@ai-sdk/openai';
import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { run } from '../../lib/run';

run(async () => {
  const openai = createOpenAI();

  const result = await openai.transcription('gpt-transcribe').doGenerate({
    audio: await readFile('data/galileo.mp3'),
    mediaType: 'audio/mpeg',
    providerOptions: {
      openai: { responseFormat: 'json', timestampGranularities: [] },
    },
  });

  console.dir({
    responseBody: result.response.body,
    language: result.language,
    providerMetadata: result.providerMetadata,
  }, { depth: null });
});
```

</details>

